            <div xml:id="d492">

                <pb facs="0746" n="630" sameAs="frus:frus1923v01/pg630"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.003 C 73/105: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Schurman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-12-14T15:00:00+08:00"><hi rendition="#italic">December 14,
                                1923—3 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received December 14—12:45
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>400. Your 247, December 13 [<hi rendition="#italic">12</hi>], 5 p.m.<anchor
                        n="69" xml:id="d492-f1"/> Chinese Foreign Office has just replied by
                    memorandum, dated December 13th, consenting to postponement of convening
                    Extraterritoriality Commission at Peking to November 1st, 1924. Foreign Office
                    states that it is telegraphing to Chinese Minister at Washington to take this
                    matter up with the American Government and expresses the hope that nature of the
                    replies of the various Governments will be transmitted to Chinese Government as
                    they are received.</p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                    >Bell</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
